=== btrfs ===
USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  btrfs [global] <group> [<group>...] <command> [<args>]


POSITIONALS (3) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  group
  command
  args


FLAGS (7) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Global options
    --format <format>  if supported, print subcommand output in that format
                       (text, json)
-v, --verbose          increase verbosity of the subcommand
-q, --quiet            print only errors
    --log <level>      set log level (default, info, verbose, debug, quiet)
    --dry-run          if supported, do not do any active/changing actions

Options for the main command only ──────────────────────────────────────────
    --help             print condensed help for all subcommands
    --version          print version string

=== btrfs balance ===

=== btrfs balance start ===
Balance chunks across the devices

=== btrfs balance pause ===
Pause running balance

=== btrfs balance cancel ===
Cancel running or paused balance

=== btrfs balance resume ===
Resume interrupted balance

=== btrfs balance status ===
Show status of running or paused balance

=== btrfs check ===
Check structural integrity of a filesystem (unmounted).

=== btrfs device ===

=== btrfs device add ===
Add one or more devices to a mounted filesystem.

=== btrfs device delete ===
Remove a device from a filesystem

=== btrfs device remove ===
Remove a device from a filesystem

=== btrfs device replace ===
Replace a device (alias of "btrfs replace")

=== btrfs device scan ===
Scan or forget (unregister) devices of btrfs filesystems

=== btrfs device ready ===
Check and wait until a group of devices of a filesystem is ready for mount

=== btrfs device stats ===
Show device IO error statistics

=== btrfs device usage ===
Show detailed information about internal allocations in devices.

=== btrfs filesystem ===

=== btrfs filesystem df ===
Show space usage information for a mount point

=== btrfs filesystem du ===
Summarize disk usage of each file.

=== btrfs filesystem show ===
Show the structure of a filesystem

=== btrfs filesystem sync ===
Force a sync on a filesystem

=== btrfs filesystem defragment ===
Defragment a file or a directory

=== btrfs filesystem resize ===
Resize a filesystem

=== btrfs filesystem label ===
Get or change the label of a filesystem

=== btrfs filesystem usage ===
Show detailed information about internal filesystem usage .

=== btrfs filesystem mkswapfile ===
Create a new file that's suitable and formatted as a swapfile.

=== btrfs inspect-internal ===

=== btrfs inspect-internal inode-resolve ===
Get file system paths for the given inode

=== btrfs inspect-internal logical-resolve ===
Get file system paths for the given logical address

=== btrfs inspect-internal subvolid-resolve ===
Get file system paths for the given subvolume ID.

=== btrfs inspect-internal rootid ===
Get tree ID of the containing subvolume of path.

=== btrfs inspect-internal map-swapfile ===
Print physical offset of first block and resume offset if file is suitable
as swapfile

=== btrfs inspect-internal min-dev-size ===
Get the minimum size the device can be shrunk to

=== btrfs inspect-internal dump-tree ===
Dump tree structures from a given device

=== btrfs inspect-internal dump-super ===
Dump superblock from a device in a textual form

=== btrfs inspect-internal tree-stats ===
Print various stats for trees

=== btrfs property ===

=== btrfs property get ===
Get a property value of a btrfs object

=== btrfs property set ===
Set a property on a btrfs object

=== btrfs property list ===
Lists available properties with their descriptions for the given object

=== btrfs qgroup ===

=== btrfs qgroup assign ===
Assign SRC as the child qgroup of DST.

=== btrfs qgroup remove ===
Remove the relation between child qgroup SRC from DST.

=== btrfs qgroup create ===
Create a subvolume quota group.

=== btrfs qgroup clear-stale ===
Clear all stale qgroups (level 0/subvolid), without a subvolume.

=== btrfs qgroup destroy ===
Destroy a quota group.

=== btrfs qgroup show ===
List subvolume quota groups.

=== btrfs qgroup limit ===
Set the limits a subvolume quota group.

=== btrfs quota ===

=== btrfs quota enable ===
Enable subvolume quota support for a filesystem.

=== btrfs quota disable ===
Disable subvolume quota support for a filesystem.

=== btrfs quota rescan ===
Trash all qgroup numbers and scan the metadata again with the current
config.

=== btrfs receive ===
Receive subvolumes from a stream

=== btrfs replace ===

=== btrfs replace start ===
Replace device of a btrfs filesystem.

=== btrfs replace status ===
Print status and progress information of a running device replace operation

=== btrfs replace cancel ===
Cancel a running device replace operation.

=== btrfs rescue ===

=== btrfs rescue chunk-recover ===
Recover the chunk tree by scanning the devices one by one.

=== btrfs rescue super-recover ===
Recover bad superblocks from good copies

=== btrfs rescue zero-log ===
Clear the tree log. Usable if it's corrupted and prevents mount.

=== btrfs rescue fix-device-size ===
Re-align device and super block sizes. Usable if newer kernel refuse to
mount it due to mismatch super size

=== btrfs rescue create-control-device ===
Create /dev/btrfs-control (see 'CONTROL DEVICE' in btrfs(5))

=== btrfs rescue clear-ino-cache ===
remove leftover items pertaining to the deprecated inode cache feature

=== btrfs rescue clear-space-cache ===
completely remove the v1 or v2 free space cache

=== btrfs rescue clear-uuid-tree ===
Delete uuid tree so that kernel can rebuild it at mount time

=== btrfs restore ===
Try to restore files from a damaged filesystem (unmounted)

=== btrfs scrub ===

=== btrfs scrub start ===
Start a new scrub. If a scrub is already running, the new one fails.

=== btrfs scrub cancel ===
Cancel a running scrub

=== btrfs scrub resume ===
Resume previously canceled or interrupted scrub

=== btrfs scrub status ===
Show status of running or finished scrub

=== btrfs scrub limit ===
Show or set scrub limits on devices of the given filesystem.

=== btrfs send ===
Send the subvolume(s) to stdout.

=== btrfs subvolume ===

=== btrfs subvolume create ===
Create subvolume(s)

=== btrfs subvolume delete ===
Delete subvolume(s)

=== btrfs subvolume list ===
List subvolumes and snapshots in the filesystem.

=== btrfs subvolume snapshot ===

=== btrfs subvolume get-default ===
Get the default subvolume of a filesystem

=== btrfs subvolume set-default ===
Set the default subvolume of the filesystem mounted as default.

=== btrfs subvolume find-new ===
List the recently modified files in a filesystem

=== btrfs subvolume show ===
Show more information about the subvolume (UUIDs, generations, times,
snapshots)

=== btrfs subvolume sync ===
Wait until given subvolume(s) are completely removed from the filesystem.

=== btrfs help ===
Display help information

=== btrfs version ===
Display btrfs-progs version
